[[:db/retract 17592186086622 :answer-field/choices 17592186086624] [:db/retract 17592186086622 :answer-field/choices 17592186086625] [:db/retract 17592186086622 :answer-field/choices 17592186086626] [:db/retract 17592186086622 :answer-field/choices 17592186086627] [:db/retract 17592186086622 :answer-field/choices 17592186086623] {:db/id 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8acd81a-262e-5e50-9f4c-47aaba5914d2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7b363072-76f6-5390-bc66-85c8817596a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8acd81a-262e-5e50-9f4c-47aaba5914d2" :question/id #uuid "e8acd81a-262e-5e50-9f4c-47aaba5914d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-115292" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5fb5b518fb7d0c6246934d46e635d901172c4fe215c42572895658700333dd41.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-6,-5),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-6))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-5))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a93c3c82-7336-597e-b4f9-d1528386c54a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a93c3c82-7336-597e-b4f9-d1528386c54a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a93c3c82-7336-597e-b4f9-d1528386c54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80c6c20e-5d10-5d7c-9b57-0b7f14af2045" :answer-field/choices ["answer-088d09ea-36cc-5829-be38-b18316f40985" "answer-80c6c20e-5d10-5d7c-9b57-0b7f14af2045" "answer-c9e53d3c-5186-5f38-a155-6a06ba388718" "answer-6a2b0f31-f799-5b50-b58e-38a442ee009a" "answer-7cde307b-7e0b-5c7d-9ac3-d4c2784cab98"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-088d09ea-36cc-5829-be38-b18316f40985" :answer/id #uuid "088d09ea-36cc-5829-be38-b18316f40985" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80c6c20e-5d10-5d7c-9b57-0b7f14af2045" :answer/id #uuid "80c6c20e-5d10-5d7c-9b57-0b7f14af2045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e53d3c-5186-5f38-a155-6a06ba388718" :answer/id #uuid "c9e53d3c-5186-5f38-a155-6a06ba388718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a2b0f31-f799-5b50-b58e-38a442ee009a" :answer/id #uuid "6a2b0f31-f799-5b50-b58e-38a442ee009a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cde307b-7e0b-5c7d-9ac3-d4c2784cab98" :answer/id #uuid "7cde307b-7e0b-5c7d-9ac3-d4c2784cab98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088328 :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186086622 :answer-field/correct "answer-7e8d77ae-7180-55f8-b376-5571c4c0492e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c0317ec-15cf-5656-874c-96868828130c" "answer-51734aba-06c8-5306-bece-99ceb641c594" "answer-ec80d1e3-5f96-55ec-97be-a14b4ebc5528" "answer-58828ed3-890a-5a52-8266-e15f59d9d2d3" "answer-7e8d77ae-7180-55f8-b376-5571c4c0492e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c0317ec-15cf-5656-874c-96868828130c" :answer/id #uuid "5c0317ec-15cf-5656-874c-96868828130c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51734aba-06c8-5306-bece-99ceb641c594" :answer/id #uuid "51734aba-06c8-5306-bece-99ceb641c594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec80d1e3-5f96-55ec-97be-a14b4ebc5528" :answer/id #uuid "ec80d1e3-5f96-55ec-97be-a14b4ebc5528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58828ed3-890a-5a52-8266-e15f59d9d2d3" :answer/id #uuid "58828ed3-890a-5a52-8266-e15f59d9d2d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e8d77ae-7180-55f8-b376-5571c4c0492e" :answer/id #uuid "7e8d77ae-7180-55f8-b376-5571c4c0492e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b363072-76f6-5390-bc66-85c8817596a8" :question/id #uuid "7b363072-76f6-5390-bc66-85c8817596a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-16554" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7659f73c533e9407c14ff33f65cac776eef234fd8f696b14eed4d5d288ebab1.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2702a648-2e03-505a-be81-cc9395ed7417"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2702a648-2e03-505a-be81-cc9395ed7417" :answer-field/id #uuid "2702a648-2e03-505a-be81-cc9395ed7417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-508479a4-483b-5088-be5e-ede9dc4e14b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee690150-4af4-5958-b6ba-047a5cc3a472" "answer-003a3cdb-6961-5ffb-8ced-5a7eeb3a8d25" "answer-7bbf5087-ef93-51b0-81af-75c679128295" "answer-ca0d327d-d188-553c-8472-29849d799fd9" "answer-508479a4-483b-5088-be5e-ede9dc4e14b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee690150-4af4-5958-b6ba-047a5cc3a472" :answer/id #uuid "ee690150-4af4-5958-b6ba-047a5cc3a472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-003a3cdb-6961-5ffb-8ced-5a7eeb3a8d25" :answer/id #uuid "003a3cdb-6961-5ffb-8ced-5a7eeb3a8d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bbf5087-ef93-51b0-81af-75c679128295" :answer/id #uuid "7bbf5087-ef93-51b0-81af-75c679128295" :answer/type :answ